<p>Grim and poignant. Very good.</p>
<p>You captured the voices of those irl people perfectly. A lot of writers here are let down by the unrealistic dialogue in their pieces; it's been a while since I read dialogue as convincing as yours on this site. You should produce a guide on how to write it, if you can.</p>
<p>I felt slightly let down by the ending, because you could have done more with the excellent narrative base. It's a tad rushed and sparse. It relies on subtle-ish implications, which feels intellectually neat, but can lead to confusion (as evidenced above in these comments) and is emotionally weaker. I would have been more affected by this if you'd been more explicit in describing the breakdown of services across the globe, and how people (esp. individuals) had been affected <em>emotionally</em> by the catastrophe. A journal entry or interview log, or something similar. It felt quite abstract. Taking the time to describe a few specific events affecting specific characters (with more than a one-line &quot;I buried [FACELESS NAME] today&quot;) would have brought me in deeper into the story.</p>
<p>That above paragraph is what would have elevated it from &quot;very good&quot; to &quot;great&quot;.</p>

